From: Djair Guilherme <djair.jr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: dw-axi-dmac: quiet apb_regs error in fixed-channel mode

On Sophgo CV18xx (AXI_DMA_FLAG_ARG0_AS_CHAN) the dmamux ties each request
line to a fixed channel and the controller has no handshake select
register, so dw_axi_dma_set_hw_channel() has nothing to do. It printed
"apb_regs not initialized" at every channel start and stop; keep the
error only for the other modes.

diff --color -ruN a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c
--- a/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c	2026-10-18 12:22:50.041805337 -0300
+++ b/drivers/dma/dw-axi-dmac/dw-axi-dmac-platform.c	2026-10-18 12:22:50.058480061 -0300
@@ -574,7 +574,13 @@
 	unsigned long reg_value, val;
 
 	if (!chip->apb_regs) {
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "apb_regs not initialized\n");
+		/*
+		 * With the handshake used as the channel number (Sophgo
+		 * CV18xx: the dmamux ties each request to a fixed channel)
+		 * there is no handshake select register to program.
+		 */
+		if (!chip->dw->hdata->use_handshake_as_channel_number)
+			dev_err(chip->dev, "apb_regs not initialized\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
